---
description: Run every project command inside the Docker dev container (arch-09 §7)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Containerized execution rules for Cursor (arch-09 §7)

Installed by `setup.sh --containerized` as `.cursor/rules/containerized-dev.mdc`
when Cursor is among the configured agents. The bullets can also be pasted into
the project root `.cursorrules`.

- Always execute terminal commands inside the Docker dev container. From a
  host terminal that means `docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml exec dev
  <command>`. Never run project build/test/deploy commands directly on the host.
- When the terminal is already inside the dev container — Cursor attached via
  `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json`, `/.dockerenv` exists, or the workspace is
  mounted at `/workspace` — run commands directly. Do not nest `docker compose
  exec` there: the container has no Docker socket, so it cannot reach a daemon.
- Prefer `/workspace` as the absolute path root for all file operations inside
  the container.
- Before running a batch of unattended, destructive-capable commands, create a
  git checkpoint (a commit or `git stash`) so the run is instantly recoverable
  (arch-09 §6).
